<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#corvee-labour">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Corvée labour</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as corvée</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Corvée labour is unpaid work required by a state from its subjects, often for building and maintaining public works or for military service. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Han Dynasty</a> imposed labour obligations on its peasant population, following the punishing demands that had destroyed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-empire">Khmer Empire</a> mobilised corvée labour for its temples, irrigation works and armies.</p></div>
